quiz:{
 tag:'Quiz',title:['How much do you know about ','the nuclear world?'],sub:'12 quick questions. Don’t worry: each answer comes with a short explanation.',
 q:'Question',of:'of',next:'Next →',again:'↺ Retake the quiz',result:'Your score',msgs:['Good start! Browse the site and try again.','Nice work! You are on the right track.','Excellent! You have strong nuclear knowledge.','Amazing! You are a true nuclear expert 🏆'],
 items:[['What does the word “nuclear” mean?',['Related to electricity','Related to the nucleus of the atom','Related to the Sun','Related to weapons only'],1,'“Nuclear” comes from “nucleus”, the center of the atom.'],
 ['What determines which element an atom is?',['Number of neutrons','Number of free electrons','Number of protons','Size of the atom'],2,'The number of protons (atomic number) distinguishes one element from another.'],
 ['What is a half-life?',['Half the career of a plant worker','The time for half of a radioactive material to decay','Half the time a reactor runs','The time for fuel to melt'],1,'After one half-life, half remains; after two, a quarter; and so on.'],
 ['Which barrier is enough to stop alpha particles?',['A sheet of paper','Only thick lead','One meter of concrete','Nothing stops them'],0,'Alpha particles are heavy and are stopped by paper or the outer layer of skin.'],
 ['What is the best shield against neutrons?',['Paper','Aluminum','Water or concrete','Glass'],2,'Hydrogen-rich materials like water slow down and stop neutrons efficiently.'],
 ['What do control rods do in a reactor?',['Cool the water','Absorb neutrons to control power','Generate electricity','Enrich the fuel'],1,'Inserting rods absorbs neutrons and lowers power; withdrawing them raises it.'],
 ['Can a nuclear reactor explode like a nuclear bomb?',['Yes, if it overheats','Yes, during earthquakes','No, its fuel is low-enriched','Yes, if the pumps stop'],2,'Reactor fuel is only 3–5% enriched and cannot cause a nuclear explosion.'],
 ['What is the ALARA principle?',['Maximum possible power','Keep doses as low as reasonably achievable','Fastest possible startup','Highest possible enrichment'],1,'Its three tools: less time, more distance, and shielding.'],
 ['If you double your distance from a point radiation source, the dose becomes:',['Half','A quarter','Double','The same'],1,'By the inverse-square law: (1/2)² = 1/4.'],
 ['Which of these naturally contains a radioactive substance?',['Bananas','Distilled water','Gold','Glass'],0,'Bananas contain radioactive potassium-40, but the dose is tiny.'],
 ['What was the main cause of the Fukushima accident?',['A mistake during a night test','Loss of cooling after an earthquake and tsunami','A terrorist attack','A nuclear explosion'],1,'The tsunami flooded the backup generators, cooling stopped, and decay heat drove temperatures up.'],
 ['What powers the Sun?',['Nuclear fission','Chemical burning','Nuclear fusion','Static electricity'],2,'In the Sun’s core, hydrogen nuclei fuse into helium and release enormous energy.']]
},

